                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 350,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why aren't we fixing exprtk instead of adding a new function?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 350,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kimi Chen",
                        "email": "kimi.zy.chen@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "zuyan-kimi"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Patrick,\nThank you for reviewing it.\nI did submit a PR to ExprTk to fix this issue, but the maintainer closed it. His reasoning was based on C++'s 'zero-overhead principle'\u2014adding a NaN check to inrange would impose a cost on all users, including those who can guarantee their inputs are never NaN. Therefore, I decided to handle it here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 350,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I made another attempt an an upstream fix.  I don't think his \"zero-overhead principle\" argument applies to the change that I made (because it actually made his benchmark slightly faster in my case).\n\nhttps://github.com/ArashPartow/exprtk/pull/54"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 350,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kimi Chen",
                        "email": "kimi.zy.chen@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "zuyan-kimi"
                    },
                    "message": "Your fix is an excellent approach to handling the NaN values with no overhead. \nI hadn't considered this solution before. \nI truly appreciate your idea\u2014thank you!"
                }
            ],
